{"event": "editor_note", "time": 1791883095.024, "text": "All five seeds (12, 22, 28, 29, 33) pass with zero violations. Here is the complete summary:\n\n---\n\n## Repaired Issues\n\n### Bug 1 \u2014 `executor.py` line 78: `_report` loop guarded on `lease.lost` instead of `lease.valid()`\n\n**File:** `src/jobrouter/executor.py`  \n**Change:** `while lease.lost is None:` \u2192 `while lease.valid():`\n\n**Root cause:** `lease.lost` is set to `\"expired\"` only when the renew task next wakes up \u2014 up to `RENEW_INTERVAL_S + RENEW_TIMEOUT_S` = 0.9 s after the lease actually ran out (longer during a node pause). During that gap, the report-retry loop kept sending `report` RPCs under an expired lease, violating **A3** (\"a holder never acts after its lease expires\"). `lease.valid()` checks both `lost is None` AND `clock.now() < valid_until`, so it catches expiry immediately. The `_execute` poll loop at line 60 already used `lease.valid()` correctly; `_report` was inconsistent with it. The runbook (`lease-overlap.md` \u00a71) explicitly names this anti-pattern.\n\n### Bug 2 \u2014 `releaser.py` line 92: capacity freed after `release` reply, not after `ReleaseComplete`\n\n**File:** `src/jobrouter/releaser.py`  \n**Change:** Moved `self._on_freed(key, op_id)` from immediately after `_request()` to after the `while via is None` loop (i.e., after `ReleaseComplete` is confirmed).\n\n**Root cause:** The GPU API contract (`gpu-api-v3.md` \u00a73.4) requires: \"Callers that track free units must not count them free until `ReleaseComplete`.\" The `capacity.py` docstring also states units stay reserved \"until the router has observed ReleaseComplete.\" Calling `_on_freed` right after the `release` RPC reply freed units while the GPU still counted them committed, allowing new submits to push GPU-committed units above capacity (CAPACITY errors). This bug was masked by Bug 1 in the original trace (the late reports consumed capacity slots that should have been held), and only became visible once Bug 1 was fixed alone.\n\n**Both fixes are required together** \u2014 neither alone produces a clean run on all seeds."}
"}

